          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "SP 81 SE          BUCKLAND                    BUCKLAND VILLAGE                                               west side 5/46                                          Yew Tree Cottage II Cottage. C17 altered. Timber framed with red brick infill and part re-fronting. Thatched roof half-hipped to south gable, central brick chimney and one projecting from the south gable; 2 pointed eaves dormers. 1½ storeys. L-shaped with gabled wing to RH with modern bay window having tiled lean-to roof, 2 light casement above. Blocked door to LH with tiled hood, modern glazed door in centre, small bay window to RH with tiled roof, and C20 lean-to projection in angle with wing. Plaque on wall by former ioor with arms and motto of Edward Bonus, Rector, dated 1882. RCHM I. p.68. MON.4. Listing NGR: SP8868312434"
    }
  ],
